Backport of upstream commit e7054989bd67 ("cfg80211: allow passing the BSS to
cfg80211_connect_result()") into the 4.4.189 cfg80211 core, plus wiring it up in
the in-kernel Rockchip rtl8188eu driver.

Problem on RG351MP mesh roaming:
  On a roam the rtl8188eu driver re-associates to the new AP and calls
  cfg80211_connect_result(). The 4.4 core then self-looks-up the BSS via
  wdev->ssid in __cfg80211_connect_result(); after a roam that lookup can fail
  and hit WARN_ON(!bss), so wdev->current_bss is never set. The nl80211 core
  subsequently rejects the PTK, the 4-way handshake fails (WRONG_KEY) and the
  link wedges until the dongle is physically re-plugged.

Fix:
  Add cfg80211_connect_bss(), which lets the driver hand over the exact BSS it
  already knows (cur_network) so the core does not have to look it up. The
  driver fetches the target BSS with cfg80211_get_bss() using the REAL target
  SSID/BSSID (not the possibly-stale wdev->ssid) and passes it in. Fully
  backward compatible: the existing cfg80211_connect_result() path leaves
  ev->cr.bss == NULL and behaves exactly as before.

